     8→
     9→Our current parser has a quadratic performance problem with right-recursive rules:
    10→
    11→```perl
    12→# Grammar rules causing the problem:
    13→CharSeq -> Char CharSeq  # Right recursion
    14→CharSeq -> Char          # Base case
    15→```
    16→
    17→For input like `"hello"` (5 characters), the standard Earley parser creates:
    18→- **Position 0**: `CharSeq -> • Char CharSeq`
    19→- **Position 1**: `CharSeq -> Char • CharSeq` (waiting for CharSeq)
    20→- **Position 2**: `CharSeq -> Char • CharSeq` (another one waiting)  
    21→- **Position 3**: `CharSeq -> Char • CharSeq` (another one waiting)
    22→- **Position 4**: `CharSeq -> Char • CharSeq` (another one waiting)
    23→- **Position 5**: `CharSeq -> Char •` (base case completes)
